@* Exercise 090 - Supply Parameter From Query Capstone (advanced).
   Goal:   Take the page's state from the URL, so a link or a back button restores
           it - and keep up when the URL changes underneath you.
   Drills: [SupplyParameterFromQuery], its Name for a query key that differs from
           the property, an array-typed parameter for a repeated key, and the fact
           that these are re-supplied on navigation like any other parameter.
   Passes: dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~Ex090_ *@
<span id="page">@CurrentPage</span>
<span id="term">@Term</span>
<span id="tags">@string.Join(",", Tags ?? [])</span>
<span id="applied">@Applied</span>

@code {
    // TODO: bind these three to the query string. ex056 parsed the URL by hand; this
    // is the framework doing it, and it is supplied like a parameter rather than read
    // like a string.
    //   Page  <- "page". Note the property is int?, not int, and CurrentPage below
    //            supplies the fallback: an absent key does not leave the property
    //            alone, it writes default(T) over whatever was there. A property
    //            initialiser is therefore NOT a usable default here - it survives
    //            construction and is overwritten the moment the query is applied.
    //   Term  <- "q", a string.
    //   Tags  <- "tag", repeated - which needs an ARRAY-typed property; a string
    //            property would take only one of them.
    // A key whose name matches the property needs no argument; one that does not
    // needs Name.
    public int? Page { get; set; }

    private int CurrentPage => Page ?? 1;

    public string? Term { get; set; }

    public string[]? Tags { get; set; }

    /// How many times the query has been applied to this component. Not rendered by
    /// the framework for you - count it where parameters arrive.
    public int Applied { get; private set; }

    // TODO: count each time these parameters are supplied - including the times a
    // navigation supplies them again, which is what makes the values follow the URL.
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
        => throw new NotImplementedException("TODO: Ex090 - bind the query and count the applications");
}
